==================================================

Execute the following sequential phases as internal loops.
Do not skip phases. Do not start everything simultaneously.

PHASE 0 — Read-only audit, current state, risks and implementation plan.

PHASE 1 — Clip identity, explicit source-to-channel routing, account
isolation, idempotency and duplicate protection.

PHASE 2 — Remove arbitrary clip generation caps; implement unlimited
qualified candidates with safe resource-aware queues.

PHASE 3 — Intro/promotion/dead-air cleanup with context-aware cuts.
Preserve spoken subscribe/like reminders. Respect third-party branding
and rights; no deceptive watermark removal.

PHASE 4 — Non-destructive smart editing enhancement layer for Gaming,
Normal/Talking, Comedy/Reaction, Educational/Tutorial and Story content.
Existing editing configuration remains locked.

PHASE 5 — Live monitoring, rolling capture, live highlight detection,
restart recovery, safe chunk retention and live-priority scheduling.

PHASE 6 — Exact destination scheduling, multi-route upload jobs,
verification and safe public publishing gates.

PHASE 7 — Analytics collection, diagnosis, versioned learning,
future clip improvement and controlled comment system audit.

PHASE 8 — Dashboard visibility and operational controls.

PHASE 9 — Integration/regression, final status and Android verification plan.

At each phase:
- Inspect relevant code only.
- Plan the smallest safe change.
- Preserve unrelated changes.
- Implement.
- Run focused tests.
- Review diff.
- Update progress ledger.
- Verify that safety constraints remain intact.
- Stop if an unresolved blocker compromises the next phase.

Do not run huge full suites repeatedly.
Avoid duplicate tests unless a change justifies rerunning them.

